    "stem": "A 26-year-old graduate student is brought to the psychiatric clinic by his roommates because of dramatic changes in his behavior over the past 5 days. Three weeks ago, he was evaluated for severe fatigue, hypersomnia, and depressed mood, for which he was prescribed sertraline 50 mg daily. Over the past 5 days, he has slept only 1 to 2 hours per night and claims he feels 'more energized and invincible than ever before in my life.' He has spent $12,000 of his tuition money on online stock options, has begun drafting a 300-page manifesto to 'revolutionize global energy markets,' and talks incessantly without pausing. During the clinical interview, the patient is pacing around the room, wearing brightly mismatched clothing, and speaks rapidly with pressured, loud speech that is difficult to interrupt. He demonstrates flight of ideas, jumping rapidly from discussing clean energy to quantum computing to his plans to run for political office. He admits to racing thoughts and denies any depressive symptoms. Physical examination, vital signs, toxicology screen, and thyroid panel are normal. Which of the following is the most appropriate initial management step?",
